PUT vs PATCH (perfect interview answer)

👉 Tumne bola:

PUT pura resource update karta hai, PATCH partial karta hai

✔ Ye correct hai, ab isko thoda professional bana do:

🔹 PUT
Full update karta hai resource ka
Agar kuch fields missing ho → wo overwrite (null ya default) ho sakte hain
Idempotent hota hai (same request baar-baar → same result)

👉 Example:

PUT /user/1
{
  "name": "Soni",
  "age": 25
}

👉 Isme pura object replace ho jayega

🔹 PATCH
Partial update karta hai
Sirf jo fields bhejo wahi update hoti hain
Baaki data unchanged rehta hai

👉 Example:

PATCH /user/1
{
  "age": 26
}

👉 Sirf age change hogi

💬 Interview me kaise bolo (ready line)

👉 Short and strong:

“PUT is used for full resource replacement, whereas PATCH is used for partial updates. PUT is idempotent and replaces the entire object, while PATCH updates only specific fields without affecting the rest.”

⚡ Bonus point (impress karne ke liye)

👉 Agar poocha “idempotent kya hai?”

Bolna:

“Idempotent means making the same request multiple times results in the same state.”

